    "title": "Capcom Just Changed the Pragmata Release Date Yet Again",
    "text": "Off Duty Games Game Rant Published March 06, 2026 at 12:39pm ET By Sarah Fields Pragmata has gone through a tumultuous development cycle, with the game originally revealed in 2020 and planned for release in 2022. However, the game underwent multiple delays, first being pushed back to 2023, only to have an indefinite delay announced for the game that year, and later on, a new release date set for April. Thankfully, Pragmata hasn't been lost entirely, and the game now has a new official release date.Pragmata Release is Arriving Sooner Than Expected via Capcom Although Pragmata is still hiding a lot about its story, this new trailer gave a few more glimpses into what's going on and why Hugh is constantly being attacked by robots. After Hugh and Diana agree to go to Earth together \"when this is all done,\" he asks why the enemies keep trying to kill them. Diana explains that during her preparations to go to Earth, a moonquake hit and damaged IDUS, the Intelligent Direction Unification System that seems to be managing the base at large and the defenses there. With this knowledge, Hugh affirms that the two will shut IDUS down and head back to his home planet, with Diana reiterating it to an unknown entity — perhaps IDUS.A few other scenes in the video give some more ideas on the content of the game, showcasing things like what Luna Filament, a 3D printing-like building material, is capable of doing on the base. Players can also get a glimpse of more combat, hacking, and some weapons that it looks like Hugh will be able to make use of to protect the two of them, as well as a holographic cat that has made an appearance in multiple teasers. The last peek is at another AI called Cabin, which seems like a friendly tour guide for the Shelter lunar research facility. This article originally appeared on GameRant and is republished here with permission. © Copyright 2026 Game Rant. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten or redistributed. You May Also Like",
